WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.860
Grouping is used when the data we have is very large.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.840
And the groups are called class intervals.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.600
In one of our examples, we had seen groups like these.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.120
1 to 5 ,6 to 10, 11 to 15 and so on.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.060
There are a few things we need to know about class intervals.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.240
The class intervals should be non-overlapping.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.660
It means that the same number cannot be present in two or more groups.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.120
One number should belong to just one group.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.100
All the groups should exhaust all the data we have with us.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.980
These three groups are enough to cover all marks from 1 to 15.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.000
But if we had someone who scored a 16,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.160
these three groups would not be enough.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.760
Next, the class size or the class width should be the same.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.400
Class width is the difference between the two lower limits,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.140
or two upper limits of continuous class intervals.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:09.260
So 6 minus 1, should equal 11 minus 6, and 10 minus 5

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.760
and 15 minus 10 should also be equal.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.900
Remember, there shouldn't be overlapping.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.680
The intervals should cover all values in the data .

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.660
And the class width has to be the same throughout.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.500
There is just one more condition

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:31.040
we need to keep in mind. In the first interval, 1 &amp; 5 are class limits.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.700
And the average of 1 &amp; 5 is called the class mark.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.260
The fourth condition says that the class limits

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.420
and the class marks of each interval should be integers,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.720
or simple fractions.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.020
A simple fraction is a fraction

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:52.720
in which the numerator and the denominator are both integers.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.540
These are the basic rules we need to keep in mind

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.120
while making groups or class intervals.

